{"orgCode":"5227","name":"Board of State and Community Corrections","agencyCode":"5210","agencyName":"Corrections and Rehabilitation","description":"The mission of the Board of State and Community Corrections is to provide statewide leadership, coordination, and technical assistance necessary to promote effective state and local efforts and partnerships within California's adult and juvenile criminal justice systems, and to promote legal and safe conditions for youth, the incarcerated, and staff in local detention facilities. This mission reflects the principle of aligning fiscal policy and correctional practices including prevention, intervention, suppression, and supervision. The goal is to promote a justice investment strategy that fits each county and is consistent with the integrated statewide goal of improved public safety through cost-effective, promising, and evidence-based strategies for managing criminal justice populations. The Board seeks to ensure that its efforts are systematically informed by experts and stakeholders with subject matter expertise.\n\nBecause the Board of State and Community Corrections' programs drive a need for infrastructure investment, the Board has a capital outlay program to support this need. For the specifics on the Board's capital outlay program see \"Infrastructure Overview.\"","totals":{"amounts":{"py":524662,"cy":413389,"by":379919},"positions":{"py":129.3,"cy":176,"by":187},"excluded":{"nongovernmental":{"py":29320,"cy":0,"by":230667}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/5210/5227","kind":"department","name":"Board of State and Community Corrections","code":"5227","amounts":{"py":524662,"cy":413389,"by":379919},"positions":{"py":129.3,"cy":176,"by":187},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":312983,"cy":191936,"by":165961},"special":{"py":170211,"cy":157915,"by":150465},"federal":{"py":41468,"cy":63538,"by":63493}},"children":[{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4940","kind":"program","name":"Administration, Research and Program Support","code":"4940","amounts":{"py":28707,"cy":49166,"by":59100},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":28707,"cy":49166,"by":59100}},"positions":{"py":46.2,"cy":59,"by":60},"description":"4940 - ADMINISTRATION, RESEARCH AND PROGRAM SUPPORT The objective of the Administration, Research and Program Support Program is to provide policy direction, accountability, administrative oversight, and support to ensure the overall success of all Board of State and Community Corrections' programs, which include Fiscal Services, Information Technology, Operations, and Support. The Research Department is responsible for providing support to the Agency's various programs, including development of rating criteria for competitive grants, providing grantees with technical assistance for local program evaluations, conducting statewide program process and outcome evaluations, and collecting data and maintaining various databases relative to the Board's responsibilities.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":28707,"cy":49166,"by":59100}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4940/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":28707,"cy":49166,"by":59100},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":28707,"cy":49166,"by":59100}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":28707,"cy":49166,"by":59100}}}}]},{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4945","kind":"program","name":"Corrections Planning and Grant Programs","code":"4945","amounts":{"py":465552,"cy":327568,"by":284135},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":253873,"cy":106115,"by":70177},"special":{"py":170211,"cy":157915,"by":150465},"federal":{"py":41468,"cy":63538,"by":63493}},"positions":{"py":36.1,"cy":44,"by":54},"description":"4945 - CORRECTIONS PLANNING AND GRANT PROGRAMS The objective of the Corrections Planning and Grant Programs (CPGP) Division is to provide leadership in the development, administration, and evaluation of state and federally funded grant programs awarded to community-based organizations, state and local governments, and tribes. CPGP administers a broad portfolio of grant programs designed to address public health and safety needs by providing mental health and substance use disorder treatment, education, intervention, diversion, housing and reentry services, and community-based violence reduction efforts. CPGP facilitates fiscal accountability and program oversight by managing fair, consistent, and effective funding and technical assistance processes.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":3092,"cy":9061,"by":8552},"Local Assistance":{"py":462460,"cy":318507,"by":275583}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4945/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":253873,"cy":106115,"by":70177},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":253873,"cy":106115,"by":70177}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":1659,"cy":2549,"by":2557},"Local Assistance":{"py":252214,"cy":103566,"by":67620}}}},{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4945/f0890","kind":"fund","name":"Federal Trust Fund","code":"0890","amounts":{"py":41468,"cy":63538,"by":63493},"byFundType":{"federal":{"py":41468,"cy":63538,"by":63493}},"extra":{"fundType":"federal","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":877,"cy":4399,"by":4354},"Local Assistance":{"py":40591,"cy":59139,"by":59139}}}},{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4945/f3354","kind":"fund","name":"Cannabis Tax Fund - Board of State and Community Corrections, State and Local Government Law Enforcement Account - Allocation 3","code":"3354","amounts":{"py":9183,"cy":42260,"by":32822},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":9183,"cy":42260,"by":32822}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":556,"cy":2113,"by":1641},"Local Assistance":{"py":8627,"cy":40147,"by":31181}}}},{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4945/f3287","kind":"fund","name":"Second Chance Fund","code":"3287","amounts":{"py":161028,"cy":59225,"by":57640},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":161028,"cy":59225,"by":57640}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":161028,"cy":59225,"by":57640}}}},{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4945/f3437","kind":"fund","name":"Gun Violence Prevention and School Safety Fund","code":"3437","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":56430,"by":60003},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":0,"cy":56430,"by":60003}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":0,"cy":56430,"by":60003}}}}]},{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4950","kind":"program","name":"Local Facility Standards and Operations","code":"4950","amounts":{"py":5324,"cy":6177,"by":6185},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":5324,"cy":6177,"by":6185}},"positions":{"py":27,"cy":30,"by":30},"description":"4950 - LOCAL FACILITY STANDARDS AND OPERATIONS\n\nThe Facilities Standards and Operations (FSO) Division works to maintain and enhance the safety, security, and efficiency of local adult and juvenile detention facilities. Specific activities of the FSO include establishing minimum standards regarding the design and operation of local adult and juvenile detention facilities (California Code of Regulations, Titles 15 and 24), conducting annual and unannounced inspections of local adult and juvenile detention facilities, and providing technical assistance and training to law enforcement, probation, and corrections agencies.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":5324,"cy":6177,"by":6185}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4950/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":5324,"cy":6177,"by":6185},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":5324,"cy":6177,"by":6185}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":5324,"cy":6177,"by":6185}}}}]},{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4952","kind":"program","name":"In-Custody Death Review Division","code":"4952","amounts":{"py":362,"cy":5299,"by":5314},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":362,"cy":5299,"by":5314}},"positions":{"py":1.8,"cy":24,"by":24},"description":"4952 - IN-CUSTODY DEATH REVIEW DIVISION\n\nThe In-Custody Death Review (ICDR) Division is a new state program responsible for reviewing investigations of deaths that occur within a local detention facility. The ICDR Division will provide recommendations to the sheriff or facility administrator related to the prevention of in-custody death and delivery of medical and behavioral health care in local detention facilities.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":362,"cy":5299,"by":5314}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4952/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":362,"cy":5299,"by":5314},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":362,"cy":5299,"by":5314}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":362,"cy":5299,"by":5314}}}}]},{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4955","kind":"program","name":"Standards and Training for Local Corrections","code":"4955","amounts":{"py":23650,"cy":23989,"by":23993},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":23650,"cy":23989,"by":23993}},"positions":{"py":12.7,"cy":13,"by":13},"description":"4955 - STANDARDS AND TRAINING FOR LOCAL CORRECTIONS\n\nThe Standards and Training for Corrections (STC) Division works in collaboration with local corrections and public/private training providers in developing and administering programs designed to ensure the competency of state and local corrections professionals. Specific activities of STC include establishing and updating minimum selection and training standards (California Code of Regulations, Title 15); assisting agencies in their efforts to meet selection and training standards; monitoring state and local corrections agencies for compliance with standards; administering a statewide training course certification process that includes a coordinated training delivery system; and providing training to corrections agencies in the areas of instructor development and curriculum design.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":2730,"cy":3019,"by":3023},"Local Assistance":{"py":20920,"cy":20970,"by":20970}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4955/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":23650,"cy":23989,"by":23993},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":23650,"cy":23989,"by":23993}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":2730,"cy":3019,"by":3023},"Local Assistance":{"py":20920,"cy":20970,"by":20970}}}}]},{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4965","kind":"program","name":"County Facility Construction","code":"4965","amounts":{"py":1067,"cy":1190,"by":1192},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":1067,"cy":1190,"by":1192}},"positions":{"py":5.5,"cy":6,"by":6},"description":"4965 - COUNTY FACILITIES CONSTRUCTION County Facilities Construction (CFC) works with state and local government agencies to administer state financing for county facility construction projects to enhance public safety and conditions of confinement.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":1067,"cy":1190,"by":1192}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4965/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":1067,"cy":1190,"by":1192},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":1067,"cy":1190,"by":1192}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":1067,"cy":1190,"by":1192}}}}]}],"sources":[{"label":"ebudget.ca.gov API: orgProgram/5227","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/api/budget/e/2026-27/orgProgram/5227"},{"label":"Detailed Expenditures by Program (PDF)","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/2026-27/pdf/Enacted/GovernorsBudget/5210/5227.pdf"}],"extra":{"legalCitations":"DEPARTMENT AUTHORITY Penal Code, Part 3, Title 7, Chapter 5. PROGRAM AUTHORITY 4945-Corrections Planning and Grant Programs: Penal Code sections 1001.85 et seq., 1228 et seq., 6024, 6027, 6045 et seq., 6046 et seq., and 13826 et seq.; Welfare and Institutions Code sections 743 et seq., 749.2 and 749.3 et seq., 749.5 et seq., 1950 et seq., 1960 et seq., 1970 et seq., and 1980 et seq.; Government Code section 30061, and Revenue and Taxation Code section 34019. 4950-Local Facility Standards and Operations: Penal Code sections 6029-6031.6; Welfare and Institutions Code sections 207, 207.1, 208.5, 209, 210, 210.2, and 885.\n\n4952-In-Custody Death Review: Penal Code sections 832.10, 6024, and 6034 4955-Standards and Training for Local Corrections: Penal Code sections 6035-6036, and 6040. 4965-County Facilities Construction: Penal Code sections 6029-6029.1; Government Code sections 15820.90-15820.917, 15820.921-15820.926, 15820.93-15820.936, and 15820.94-15820.947; and Welfare and Institutions Code section 2250."},"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/5210/5227/4960","kind":"program","name":"Infrastructure (Capital Outlay)","code":"4960","amounts":{"py":29320,"cy":0,"by":230667},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":29320,"cy":0,"by":230667}},"description":"The Board of State and Community Corrections (BSCC) and the Department of Corrections and Rehabilitation jointly administer several programs to partially finance the design and construction of county correctional facilities. The programs consist of Adult Local Criminal Justice and Local Youth Offender Rehabilitation facilities. Legislation is comprised of the 2007 Senate Bill 81 (Youth), the 2007 Assembly Bill 900 (Adult), the 2012 Senate Bill 1022 (Adult), the 2014 Senate Bill 863 (Adult), and the 2016 Senate Bill 844 (Adult). A total of $294 million has been awarded to 18 projects across the counties to build or remodel Youth Offender facilities and $2.057 billion has been awarded to 52 projects across the counties to build or remodel Adult Local Criminal Justice facilities. BSCC oversees 29 of these projects totaling $918 million authorized from Senate Bill 1022, Senate Bill 863, and Senate Bill 844. BSCC currently has $20 million remaining to be awarded from Senate Bill 863 and $1.3 million remaining to be awarded from Senate Bill 1022.","extr